    "created_at": "2016-08-02T14:18:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-02T14:18:57Z",
    "body": "Yes, exactly. Just like some browsers display [a calendar](https://pixplusteam.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Screenshot_2016-01-19-20-23-49.png) for `<input type=\"date\">` and others display [a series of spinners](http://blog.teamtreehouse.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/date.png), browsers can choose different implementations of the datalist control. This is a good way to encourage innovation, as browsers can experiment with new patterns in ways that might help users more. For example, if I were you I'd file a bug on Chrome asking them to add the more user-friendly full text search matching!\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
